cachy-asahi-update is an independent DEVELOPMENT packaging candidate, not a
supported Apple updater or an official CachyOS release.

Software: CachyOS/cachy-update commit e2b1b7144be71cf392809f48d1440f8da1d9c81a,
a fork of Robin Candau's Arch-Update. Preserve its GPL-3.0-or-later grant,
copyright/SPDX notices and translation credits. The package retains the complete
updater and compiled tray functionality, but enables no service or autostart.

Modified 2026-10-11 by cachy-asahi contributors: sanitized the source artwork and
substituted original update/status icons; changed notification launching to
quoted argv, propagated timer activation failure, required opt-in before
interactive Flatpak cleanup, and moved upgrade locking into a validated private
runtime directory with mandatory exclusivity. Modified shell files carry dated
notices in behavior.patch and retain their upstream GPL-3.0-or-later grants.

Integrated 2026-10-12 by cachy-asahi contributors: added the original MIT
read-only asahi-policy.py helper and apple-policy.patch. The latter modifies
update.sh, full_upgrade.sh, kernel_reboot.sh and restart_services.sh to require
caller-pinned protected platform/module transitions before updater operations,
replace the PC vmlinuz heuristic, and filter protected service restart requests.
These GPL-3.0-or-later shell modifications retain their dated 2026-10-11 source
notices. No accepted target policy, hardware approval or coordinated update
controller is supplied by this source integration. The MIT helper copyright is
held by cachy-asahi contributors (2026); its full MIT grant is installed as
PROJECT-MIT (the same project grant used in ICON-LICENSE). This compatible grant
does not relicense the upstream GPL-3.0-or-later software.

All ten upstream Cachy-branded SVG files are excluded from the sanitized source
because their artwork provenance/grant was not established by this audit.
Nine independently authored geometric update/status icons replace the installed
icons under the same filenames. These original project SVGs are MIT licensed
by cachy-asahi contributors (2026); see ICON-LICENSE. No excluded asset is
relicensed. Software names retained in upstream UI are attribution, not a claim
of endorsement. Cargo dependencies retain their individual grants and notices.
